#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Premium, Flex, and On-Prem (through the IBM Quantum Platform API) Plan users"
" can get started with IBM Qiskit Functions for free, or can procure a "
"license from one of the partners who have contributed a function to the "
"catalog.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Request a free trial for third-party Qiskit Functions {#request-a-free-"
"trial-for-third-party-qiskit-functions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To request a free trial, navigate to the [Qiskit Functions "
"Catalog](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/functions), and explore the details "
"panel. Click `Request a free trial` and fill out information required by the"
" Functions partner, including the IBM Cloud `AccessGroupId`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Navigate to [IBM Cloud IAM](http://cloud.ibm.com/iam/groups).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Verify eligibility.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Switch your account in the menu bar on the header to one with the following "
"format: `XXXXXXX - [Organization Name]`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ensure the organization is the same as the one associated with your Premium "
"account.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you see \"[Your Name]'s Account\", you are using your _personal_ account,"
" which is not eligible for premium access.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Find your access group ID.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Click a group name.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Click **Details**.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy the access group ID. It should start with `AccessGroup-`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"install-qiskit-functions-catalog-client\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Install the Qiskit Functions Catalog client {#install-the-qiskit-functions-"
"catalog-client}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To start using Qiskit Functions, install the IBM Qiskit Functions Catalog "
"client:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Retrieve your API key from the [IBM Quantum Platform "
"dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/), and activate your Python virtual"
" environment.  See the [installation instructions](/guides/install-"
"qiskit#local) if you do not already have a virtual environment set up.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <span id=\"save-account\"></span>**If you are working in a trusted Python"
" environment (such as on a personal laptop or workstation),** use the "
"`save_account()` method to save your credentials locally. ([Skip to the next"
" step](#functions-untrusted) if you are not using a trusted environment, "
"such as a shared or public computer, to authenticate to IBM Quantum "
"Platform.)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To use `save_account()`, run `python` in your shell, then enter the "
"following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Type `exit()`. From now on, whenever you need to authenticate to the "
"service, you can load your credentials with the following:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   For example:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<span id=\"functions-untrusted\"></span>**Avoid executing code on an "
"untrusted machine or an external cloud Python environment to minimize "
"security risks.** If you must use an untrusted environment (on, for example,"
" a public computer), change your API key after each use by deleting it on "
"the [IBM Cloud API keys](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/apikeys) page to reduce "
"risk. Learn more in the [Managing user API "
"keys](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-"
"userapikey&interface=ui) topic. To initialize the service in this situation,"
" use this code:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"danger\" title=\"Protect your API key\">\n"
"**Never include your key in source code, Python scripts, or notebook files.** When sharing code with others, ensure that your API key is not embedded directly within the Python script. Instead, share the script without the key and provide instructions for securely setting it up.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you accidentally share your key with someone or include it in version control like Git, immediately revoke your key by deleting it on the [IBM Cloud API keys](https://cloud.ibm.com/iam/apikeys) page to reduce risk. Learn more in the [Managing user API keys](https://cloud.ibm.com/docs/account?topic=account-userapikey&interface=ui) topic.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "List the functions you can access {#list-the-functions-you-can-access}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After you authenticate, you can list the functions from the Qiskit Functions"
" Catalog that you have access to:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run enabled functions {#run-enabled-functions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After a catalog object has been instantiated, you can select a function by "
"using `catalog.load(\"<provider/function-name>\")`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each Qiskit Function has custom inputs, options, and outputs. Check the "
"specific documentation pages for the function you want to run for more "
"information. By default, all users can only run one function job at a "
"time:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`run()` checks your remaining capacity and backend access before it submits "
"the job. If your instance is out of capacity, or the backend you named is "
"not accessible, `run()` raises an error right away instead of leaving the "
"job to fail in the queue. When capacity is low, `run()` emits a warning. "
"Pass `suppress_low_usage_warning=True` to silence it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"check-job-status\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Check job status {#check-job-status}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With your Qiskit Function `job_id`, you can check the status of running "
"jobs. This includes the following statuses:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`QUEUED`**: The remote program is in the Qiskit Function queue. The queue "
"priority is based on how much you've used Qiskit Functions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`INITIALIZING`**: The remote program is starting; this includes setting up"
" the remote environment and installing dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`RUNNING`**: The program is running. This also includes several more "
"detailed statuses if supported by specific functions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`RUNNING: MAPPING`**: The function is currently mapping your classical "
"inputs to quantum inputs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`**: The function is optimizing for the "
"selected QPU. This could include circuit transpilation, QPU "
"characterization, observable backpropagation, and so forth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`**: The function has submitted a job to IBM "
"Quantum Compute Service, and is waiting in the queue.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU`**: The function has an active Quantum Compute "
"job.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING`**: The function is post-processing results, "
"which can include error mitigation, mapping quantum results to classical, "
"and so forth.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`DONE`**: The program is complete, and you can retrieve result data with "
"`job.result()`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`ERROR`**: The program stopped running because of a problem. Use "
"`job.result()` to get the error message.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`CANCELED`**: The program was canceled by a user, the service, or the "
"server.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"retrieve-results\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve results {#retrieve-results}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After a program is `DONE`, you can use `job.result()` to fetch the result. "
"This output format varies with each function, so be sure to follow the "
"specific documentation:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You can also cancel a job at any time:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Access the associated Quantum Compute jobs {#access-the-associated-quantum-"
"compute-jobs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Qiskit Function can submit one or more Quantum Compute jobs to a QPU while"
" it runs. To retrieve the IDs of those runtime jobs, use "
"`job.runtime_jobs()`. You can use these IDs to fetch the runtime job objects"
" from a `QiskitRuntimeService` instance, or to find the workloads on the IBM"
" Quantum&reg; Platform dashboard.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a function groups its runtime jobs into sessions or batches, use "
"`job.runtime_sessions()` to list the session IDs. Pass one session ID to "
"`job.runtime_jobs()` to return only the runtime jobs in that session:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The returned list can be empty. A function reports its runtime jobs only when it submits them through the runtime service that the function receives at run time, and some functions do not submit runtime jobs directly.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "View job logs {#view-job-logs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use `job.logs()` to retrieve the log output that a function produces while "
"it runs. Logs are useful for tracking progress and for debugging a job that "
"ends in an `ERROR` state.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a long-running job that produces many log lines, use "
"`job.filtered_logs()` to return only the lines you want. Pass a regular "
"expression to `include` to keep matching lines, or to `exclude` to drop "
"matching lines:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"List previously run Qiskit Functions jobs {#list-previously-run-qiskit-"
"functions-jobs}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You can use `jobs()` to list all jobs submitted to Qiskit Functions:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To narrow the results, pass filters. Filter by function with `function`, by "
"status with `status`, and by submission date with `created_after`. Page "
"through results with `limit` and `offset`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you already have the job ID for a certain job, you can retrieve the job "
"with `catalog.job()`:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Fetch error messages {#fetch-error-messages}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a program status is `ERROR`, use `job.error_message()` to fetch the error"
" message as follows:\n"
msgstr ""

